\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-1)}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{1}=-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{3\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1}{(-3)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535498 17592186045443 true] [17592186488404 1071 "Consider the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $B$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular" 13194139535498 17592186045443 false] [17592186488404 1071 "Consider the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $B$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular" 13194139535498 17592186045443 true] [17592186488404 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{ali